You are Einstein's improvement executor for TESSERA Round 3 candidate R3-08.

## Goal
Speed up BM25 document-frequency counting in artifacts/api-server/src/lib/hybrid-retrieval.ts. Current code does for each query term:
`df[t] = tokenized.filter((d) => d.includes(t)).length;`
which is O(|q| * N * avgDocLen) because `Array.includes` on token arrays scans. Replace with a single O(total tokens) pass that builds df for query terms only (or all terms).

## Current bm25Scores fragment
```
  const df: Record<string, number> = {};
  for (const t of qTerms) {
    df[t] = tokenized.filter((d) => d.includes(t)).length;
  }
```

## Change to (same numeric results)
```
  const qSet = new Set(qTerms);
  const df: Record<string, number> = Object.fromEntries(qTerms.map((t) => [t, 0]));
  for (const d of tokenized) {
    const seen = new Set<string>();
    for (const w of d) {
      if (qSet.has(w) && !seen.has(w)) {
        seen.add(w);
        df[w]++;
      }
    }
  }
```

Keep idf/scoring formulas identical. Also optionally build per-doc term counts once (already done inside the map callback) — fine to leave that as-is if df fix alone is enough.

## Measure
Add artifacts/api-server/src/__tests__/hybrid-bm25-df.test.ts:
1. Export `bm25Scores` for testing OR duplicate a tiny pure copy — prefer exporting `export function bm25Scores` (it's currently not exported; exporting is OK).
2. Correctness: on a fixed corpus of ≥20 real strings from docs (read a markdown file), assert new scores deep-equal (or within 1e-12) a reference implementation that uses the OLD filter-based df.
3. Speed: time both on a larger corpus (e.g. 500 docs × repeated paragraphs, query with 8 terms) for several iterations; assert new is faster; log `BM25_DF beforeMs=X afterMs=Y speedup=Z`.

## Constraints
- Do NOT flip enable flags; no deletes; no history rewrite
- Do NOT change rerank / embeddings in this PR (R3-04 owns batching). If hybrid-retrieval already has batch rerank on main, leave it; only touch bm25Scores df loop.
- Branch: einstein/r3-08-hybrid-bm25-df
- NON-DRAFT PR: "Einstein R3-08: single-pass BM25 df in hybrid-retrieval"
- Await CI; do NOT merge
- Return PR URL, CI, timing + equality check

